foreign  [Music]  you will learn how to diagnose issues  with anthos cluster running on VMware  you can use gke CTL command line utility  to diagnose issues with your anthos  cluster on VMware first let's understand  what gke CTL is and how it can be used  to diagnose cluster issues well this is  a command line utility that interacts  with your cluster running on VMware to  perform administrative tasks and health  checks on VMware GK CTL perform health  checks related to vsphere infrastructure  node pools load balancers control plane  components user workloads and many more  components on both anthos admin and user  clusters  all right now let's learn how to use gke  CTL on VMware to diagnose the issues  with our admin cluster first login to  the admin workstation of your cluster  running on VMware then execute the  displayed command  this command performs connectivity test  between control plane components and  cluster cluster health checks and  infrastructure health checks it provides  the results for each of these tests and  finally displays the overall health of  the cluster in our example we are  getting success messages for each of the  health checks and the last line states  that the cluster is healthy woohoo this  indicates that our Vital health checks  have been passed and there are no issues  with their cluster  let's look at another output that shows  some failures the message here states  that container load balancer is  unhealthy scroll down to view if there  are any further clues for the failure  the error States fail to pull the image  this typically happens if the correct  image name is not specified in the  deployment yaml file this is a familiar  error where the image is unable to be  pulled correctly  to fix the issue view the load balancers  deployment configuration  verify the image name in the yaml oops  the image is indeed wrong which is the  reason for the failure we will update  the correct image name and version once  the file is saved it will redeploy with  the updated configuration let's re-run  the diagnose command now  congratulations we have fixed the issue  with the global load balancer and our  cluster is healthy again you can use the  same command to troubleshoot the user  cluster by passing the user cluster name  as shown here you will get a similar  output containing the help check status  for individual components and overall  health of the cluster  if the diagnose results from GK CDL  command are not sufficient to determine  the root cause and or fix the cluster  issues then you can create the snapshot  of the cluster are you wondering what a  snapshot is a snapshot is a tar file  that contains the configuration files  and logs for the cluster  please note that snapshot is an  important artifact that helps Google  Cloud perform a deep type analysis and  help resolve the issues with your  cluster  remember to share the snapshot to Google  Cloud support as part of your support  case use this command to create the  snapshot for a VMware cluster keep in  mind the command not only saves the  snapshot to your local disk it also  uploads a snapshot to the storage bucket  where we have provided access to the  Google Cloud support team before running  the diagnose snapshot command complete  these prerequisites to create and share  the snapshot enable storage API in the  fleet host project using this command  Grant the storage admin role to the  service account on its parent project  Grant read-only access of the storage  bucket to the dedicated service account  provided by the Google Cloud support  team  all right we are all set let's run the  command now  we'll now use the same command along  with the name of user cluster to create  the snapshot for a user cluster once the  snapshot is shared with Google Cloud  support team they will examine the  content of the snapshot along with the  available logs and metrics in the Google  Cloud project using this information  Google will work to provide a timely  solution congratulations you now know  how to diagnose issues with your anthos  cluster on VMware Additionally you know  how to share a snapshot in situations  where the diagnostic do not help for  more information on troubleshooting  anthos cluster running on VMware check  out this documentation thanks for  watching foreign  [Music]

